<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nome</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A nome was an administrative province of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, each governed by an official known to historians as a nomarch. Egypt was traditionally divided into some forty nomes along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> valley and delta. In the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> provincial governors administered the nome districts, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> was governed separately by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-kush">Viceroy of Kush</a>.</p></div>
